{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 resulted in TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received with FAIL 0xdead instead of a received byte. recv_buf_valid never asserts because recv_state never reaches state 10 (lines 89-94) to latch recv_pattern. Root cause is line 99 `recv_state <= recv_state + 0;` in default data-bit state (lines 96-102) which stalls the receiver instead of advancing with +1; CONE_SLICE has coverage 0/1 with only spiflash/system refs so trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 			default: begin
 				if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 					recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
-					recv_state <= recv_state + 0;
+					recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, uart loopback byte 0xa5 received with no timeout trap"}

